**, and **Wednesday**. He read:\n\n- **Monday**: First book with **20 pages**\n- **Tuesday**: Second book with **12 pages**\n- **Wednesday**: Third book with **unknown number of pages**\n\nLet the number of pages in the third book be $ x $.\n\nWe are told that **he has read a total of 51 pages from Monday to Wednesday**, which we can express as:\n\n$$\n20 \\ (\\text{Monday}) + 12 \\ (\\text{Tuesday}) + x \\ (\\text{Wednesday}) = 51\n$$\n\nNow we solve for $ x $:\n\n$$\n20 + 12 + x = 51\n$$\n$$\n32 + x = 51\n$$\n$$\nx = 51 - 32 = 19\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer**  \nThe number of pages Nico read on Wednesday is $\\boxed{19}$.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Nico borrows 3 books from the library on Monday.  On Monday, he reads the first book with a total of 20 pages.  On Tuesday, he reads the second book with a total of 12 pages.  On Wednesday, he reads the third book.  If he has read a total of 51 pages from Monday to Wednesday, how many pages did he read on Wednesday?", "answer": "From Monday to Tuesday, Nico reads a total of 20 + 12 = <<20+12=32>>32 pages.\nOn Wednesday, he read a total of 51 - 32 = <<51-32=19>>19 pages.\n#### 19", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Nico borrows 3 books from the library on Monday.  On Monday, he reads the first book with a total of 20 pages.  On Tuesday, he reads the second book with a total of 12 pages.  On Wednesday, he reads the third book.  If he has read a total of 51 pages from Monday to Wednesday, how many pages did he read on Wednesday?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["19"], "solution": "19"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 74035, 31632, 1811, 220, 18, 6467, 504, 279, 6733, 389, 7014, 13, 220, 1913, 7014, 11, 566, 15804, 279, 1156, 2311, 448, 264, 2790, 315, 220, 17, 15, 6816, 13, 220, 