d 25 seeds per row, I should multiply 4 by 25. Let me check that. 4 times 25. Well, 20 times 25 is 500, and 4 times 25 is 100, so 500 + 100 equals 600. So, the top bed can hold 600 seeds.\n\nNext, the medium bed has 3 rows with 20 seeds each. Let me calculate that. 3 rows multiplied by 20 seeds per row. 3 times 20 is 60. So, the medium bed has 60 seeds. \n\nNow, the total seeds across all four beds would be the sum of the seeds in the top bed and the medium bed. Adding 600 and 60 together. 600 plus 60 is 660. \n\nWait, but hold on. Let me double-check to make sure I didn't make a unit conversion error. The problem says the top bed can hold 4 rows with 25 seeds per row. The medium bed has 3 rows with 20 seeds each. Multiplying 4 * 25 is indeed 100, and 3 * 20 is 60. Adding 100 + 60 gives 160. Wait, hold on, that's different. Wait, earlier I thought it was 600 and 60, so total 660. Now, my math says 4 times 25 is 100? Wait, no, wait. Wait, 25 rows? Or 4 rows? Wait, the problem says \"4 rows of lettuce with 25 seeds being sown per row.\" So per row, 25 seeds. So 4 rows would be 4 multiplied by 25, which is 100. Then the medium bed is 3 rows times 20 seeds each, which is 60. So total seeds would be 100 + 60, which is 160. But in my first calculation I thought 4 * 25 was 600. Wait, that was a mistake. So where did I go wrong? \n\nOh, okay, so 25 seeds per row times 4 rows equals 100 seeds in the top bed. Oh, so earlier I added 600 and 60 but that was wrong. So actually, the total would be 100 + 60 = 160. So the answer would be 160 seeds.\n\nBut let me check again. Let's recalculate. \n\nTop bed: 4 rows * 25 seeds = 100 seeds. \n\nMedium bed: 3 rows * 20 seeds = 60 seeds. \n\nTotal: 100 + 60 = 160. \n\nYes, so that's correct. My initial mistake was thinking 4 * 25 was 600, which was wrong. I need to make sure I do the multiplication correctly. \n\nSo the answer should be 160 seeds. \n\nWait, but let me check once more. Maybe I messed up the numbers. 4 times 25. Let's do 2