 matches. Then the last round has 4 matches, and he wins half. Half of 4 is 2, so he wins 2 matches in that last round. So total matches would be 12 + 2 = 14? That seems straightforward. Let me check again.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I misread \"half of the 4 matches in the last round\". So if there are 4 matches in the last round, half of that is 2. So total matches won would be 12 (first two rounds) + 2 (last round) = 14. So the answer is 14? But let me think if there's any chance I misread the numbers. The problem says \"multiple contestants\" each. But maybe the mention of \"multiple contestants\" affects something else. Wait, no, the problem says he wins all of the matches in the first two rounds, each of which had 6 matches, so each round's matches are 6. Then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. So I don't think \"multiple contestants\" is relevant here. Maybe it's just a distractor. Let me check again.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the problem meant that he won all matches in the first two rounds, each round having 6 matches, so 2×6=12. Then in the last round, 4 matches, and he wins half. So 2 matches. So total 14. Yes. Therefore, the answer is 14.\n\nBut just to make sure, let me write it out numerically:\n\nFirst two rounds: 2 rounds × 6 matches each = 12 matches.\n\nLast round: 4 matches, half of that is 2.\n\nTotal: 12 + 2 = 14. Yep.\n\nWait, is there any chance that \"wins half of the 4 matches in the last round\" means something different? Like maybe maybe the number of matches is different? For example, maybe \"half of\" refers to something else. But no, half of 4 is 2. So that's straightforward.\n\nSo the answer should be 14. So the final answer is \\boxed{14}.\n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{14}\n</think>\n\nTo determine how many matches Brendan won throughout the competition, we break down the information given in the problem:\n\n- **First two rounds**: Each round had 6 matches. Since there are 2 such rounds, the total number of matches won in this phase is:\n\n  $$\n  2 \\times 6 = 12 \\text{ matches}\n  $$\n\n- **Last round**: There are 4 matches, and Brendan wins half of them. Half of 4 is 2, so he won 2 matches in this round.\n\nAdding the matches won in both phases together:\n\n$$\n12 + 2 = 14\n$$\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion**: Brendan won a total of $\\boxed{14}$ matches throughout the competition.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?", "answer": "In the first 2 rounds, Brendan wins a total of 2 rounds * 6 matches per round = <<2*6=12>>12 matches.\nIn the last round, Brendan wins half of the matches which is 4 matches / 2 = <<4/2=2>>2 matches.\nThroughout the competition, Brendan has therefore won 12 + 2 = <<12+2=14>>14 matches.\n#### 14", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["14"], "solution": "14"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 55843, 702, 10636, 264, 10323, 89174, 10707, 323, 14816, 9071, 2348, 5248, 74424, 13, 1260, 14816, 678, 315, 279, 9071, 304, 279, 1156, 220, 17, 19531, 11, 1817, 315, 892, 1030, 220, 21, 9071, 11, 1221, 14816], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 773, 55843, 594, 3491, 374, 911, 47209, 700, 1246, 1657, 9071, 566, 2765, 304, 264, 10707, 13, 6771, 752, 1430, 31