 one of the friends pay?", "answer": "Silas paid half = 150/2 = <<150/2=75>>75\nRemaining bill paid by 5 friends = 75 + 10% of 150 = 75 + 15 = 90\nEach person will pay 1/5 which is 90/5 = <<90/5=18>>18\nEach friend will pay $<<18=18>>18.\n#### 18", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: The dinner bill for 6 friends came to $150. Silas said he would pay for half of the bill and the remaining friends could split the rest of the bill and leave a 10% tip for the whole meal. How many dollars will one of the friends pay?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["18"], "solution": "18"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 576, 13856, 4031, 369, 220, 21, 4780, 3697, 311, 400, 16, 20, 15, 13, 8051, 300, 1053, 566, 1035, 2291, 369, 4279, 315, 279, 4031, 323, 279, 9664, 4780, 1410, 6718, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 4031, 323], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 773, 1052, 594, 419, 3491, 1380, 264, 13856, 4031, 369, 4743, 4780, 3697, 311, 400, 16, 20, 15, 13, 8051, 300, 2727, 566, 686, 2291, 4279, 315, 279, 4031, 11, 323, 279, 9664, 3040, 4780, 686, 6718, 279, 2732, 11, 323, 1052, 594, 264, 220, 16, 15, 4, 11552, 369, 279, 4361, 15145, 13, 576, 3405, 374, 10161, 1246, 1753]}
