 would be 9 liters minus 1.5 liters. Subtracting 1.5 from 9 gives... 7.5 liters. Let me verify. 9 - 1.5 is 7.5. Yep, that checks out.\n\nNow, the total fruit punch is the sum of all the juices: orange, cherry, and apple. So, orange is 4.5, cherry is 9, and apple is 7.5. Let me add those up. 4.5 plus 9 is... 13.5, and then adding 7.5 gives 13.5 + 7.5. Let me compute that. 13.5 plus 7.5... 13.5 + 7 is 20.5, plus 0.5 more is 21 liters total. So, the total is 21 liters.\n\nWait, let me make sure I didn't mix up any steps. Let me verify again:\n\n- Orange punch: 4.5 L\n- Cherry punch: 2 * 4.5 = 9 L\n- Apple juice: 9 - 1.5 = 7.5 L\nTotal: 4.5 + 9 + 7.5. \n\nAdding them: 4.5 + 9 is 13.5, plus 7.5 is 21. Yes. \n\nI think that's it. So the answer should be 21 liters. Let me check once more if there's any possibility I misread the problem. The problem says \"twice as much cherry punch as orange,\" so yes, double of 4.5 is 9. Then subtract 1.5 from cherry punch to get apple juice. Correct. So, adding all three together gives 21 liters.\n\nI don't see any errors in my calculations. So I think the final answer is 21 liters, boxed as per instruction.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how many liters of fruit punch Sunnyvale School had, we proceed step by step by analyzing the given information and combining the volumes of each juice.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Initial Information:\n- Orange punch = 4.5 liters  \n- Cherry punch = **twice** as much orange punch →  \n  $$\n  \\text{Cherry punch} = 2 \\times 4.5 = 9 \\text{ liters}\n  $$\n- Apple juice = **1.5 liters less** than cherry punch  \n  $$\n  \\text{Apple juice} = 9 - 1.5 = 7.5 \\text{ liters}\n  $$\n\n---\n\n### 2. Total Volume of Fruit Punch:\nWe add up the volumes of all three fruits:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total fruit punch} = \\text{Orange} + \\text{Cherry} + \\text{Apple juice} = 4.5 + 9 + 7.5 = 21\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{21}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Sunnyvale School was having a picnic. They wanted to make fruit punch. They had 4.5 liters of orange punch. They had twice as much cherry punch as orange punch and 1.5 liters less of apple juice than cherry punch. When they combined all of the fruit juices together, how many liters of fruit punch did they have?", "answer": "Orange = <<4.5=4.5>>4.5 L\nCherry = 2 * 4.5 = <<2*4.5=9>>9 L\nApple = 9 - 1.5 = <<9-1.5=7.5>>7.5 L\nTotal punch = 4.5 + 9 + 7.5 = <<4.5+9+7.5=21>>21 L\nThey had 21 liters of fruit punch for the picnic.\n#### 21", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Sunnyvale School was having a picnic. They wanted to make fruit punch. They had 4.5 liters of orange punch. They had twice as much cherry punch as orange punch and 1.5 liters less of apple juice than cherry punch. When they combined all of the fruit juices together, how many liters of fruit punch did they have?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["21"], "solution": "21"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 55038, 77729, 6022, 572, 3432, 264, 54462, 13, 2379, 4829, 311, 1281, 13779, 20380, 13, 2379, 1030, 220, 19, 13, 20, 92866, 315, 18575, 20380, 13, 2379, 1030, 10917, 438, 1753, 40880, 20380, 438, 18575, 20380, 323], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 773, 358, 1184, 311, 7071, 700, 1246, 1657, 92866, 315, 13779, 20380, 55038, 77729, 6022, 1030, 979, 807, 10856, 678, 279, 64859, 13, 6771, 752, 1191, 553, 8660, 279, 3491, 3019, 553, 3019, 382, 5338, 11, 279, 3491, 2727, 807, 1030, 220, 19, 13, 20, 92866, 315, 18575, 20380, 13, 5005, 432, 33845, 429, 807, 1030, 10917, 438, 1753, 40880]}
